    "section_summary": {
      "type": "string",
      "extract_value": "This discussion section summarizes the findings of a single study on Chinese adolescent girls, which explored factors influencing intuitive eating. The study found indirect effects of online interpersonal sexual objectification (OISO) experiences on intuitive eating through broad conceptualization of beauty and body appreciation. It suggests that OISO negatively impacts intuitive eating and discusses implications for interventions focusing on critiquing appearance-focused mindsets and valuing body functionality, noting that body appreciation may act as a buffer.",
      "evidence_source": "The entire section discusses 'This study' and 'Our findings' and their implications.",
      "warning": "None"
    },
